{"kind":"request","text":"Make the commitment projection preserve the loop's moral distinctions: attribution-aware terminal states, and satisfied as terminal.","body":{"conditions":"Two projection defects erase distinctions the bootstrap contract calls morally load-bearing. First, any authorized third party may supersede a promise (fold.go decideSupersede admits the maker or any ratifier), but projectCommitments labels every retired promise reneged — so a ratifier retiring someone's promise assigns them blame the record does not support; the same shape mislabels third-party request retirement as the requester's withdrawal or cancellation. Distinguish by superseding actor: maker-retired stays reneged, third-party-retired needs its own honest label. Second, the retired-request branch precedes the report branch, so a satisfaction already declared is overwritten to cancelled when the request is later retired; satisfied must be terminal. Also stop naming a waited-on performer in withdrawn and stale rows. Add tests for withdrawn, cancelled, reneged, third-party retirement, report-withdrawal reopening, and satisfied-then-retired; none of these states currently has one. Obtain independent exact-head review before merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}